WEBVTT

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:01.371
So I'll explain this with the
most simple experiment,

00:01:01.371 --> 00:01:03.162
which is the most famous experiment,

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.871
which is basically you have a wall
with two slits and you fire

00:01:05.871 --> 00:01:08.413
an electron through the wall and the
electron will either go through

00:01:08.413 --> 00:01:11.454
the left or right and will be detected
on the reader on the other end.

00:01:11.954 --> 00:01:15.621
But every now and then, the same electron
finds itself going through both holes

00:01:15.621 --> 00:01:18.371
at the same time, and it's
detected in two places.

00:01:18.788 --> 00:01:21.829
So the same electron finds itself
in more than one place.

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:26.163
At the same time, it kind of revealed that
reality was a set of constructs.

00:01:26.204 --> 00:01:29.538
So by that, I mean we can only really
observe an abstracted or

00:01:29.538 --> 00:01:32.704
a kind of limited version of the
multiple events happening at